From e232a77702ed3bcf310fc75f4ec526ca1d8944c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincent <vincent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:31:26 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] middleware, agent plugins: an edit to a file the module
 imports is loaded (#3723, JoeyWu-tech)

A module could import files beside it, which jsmod.Compile read and
bundled, but neither loader's stamp had them: internal/middleware's and
internal/agentplug's stamp() folded only the entry file's time and size
and plugins.json. So editing only an imported file kept the old code
running until the entry or plugins.json changed, or magpie restarted, and
a fix to an import that didn't compile stayed an old load error.

jsmod.Compile now gives back the files it read besides the module, each
with its path and the time and size from just before it was read. Both
loaders keep that list per entry, and stamp() folds the current stat of
each file in it, so a changed import loads the module again. A set stamps
itself once more after loading, since only then are its imports known,
so loading doesn't repeat.

Red before the fix, a folder middleware whose entry imports names.js, the
imported file rewritten with a later time (go test -tags nogui
./internal/middleware/ ./internal/agentplug/ -run TestReloadOnImportedChange):
    middleware: reload_imports_test.go:45: an imported change didn't reload: {"model":"m1","v":"one"}
    agentplug:  reload_imports_test.go:59: an imported change didn't reload
Green after: both reload and see the new mapping and name. Packages:
middleware 31, agentplug, jsmod all pass (-race too); go vet and gofmt
clean.
